      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "LADY SADLER (2) resumes as the horse to beat after a tidy last campaign, highlighted by a BM62 win at Pakenham before she was beaten just over a length in BM66 grade on soft ground. Her Cranbourne trials were mixed, but she was an impressive winner when fresh last campaign and this shapes favourably. MYSTIC REIGN (1) looks the main danger, having won at this track and distance and bringing form around BM70 and Quality grade. Has to carry the big weight, but is the class runner here and is a track and trip winner previously. DIVINE EMPRESS (6) was only run down late at Bairnsdale and gets weight relief with Damian Lane taking over, making her a genuine danger if she holds that form. TAPO (3) can take up the running and give them something to catch.",
